# The walker screen through the demo beats, against the FAKE cloud (test/EXPECTED.md, D14).
# Run (from devices/pi): WALKER_FAKE_TURN_MS=1500 node dist/walker.mjs simulate --screen --script test/sim/screen-beats.walk
# (the delay makes the fake cloud take 1.5 s per turn, so "One moment" stays up long enough to see)
# and open the printed http://127.0.0.1:8740/ at 800x480 to watch. The waits keep each screen up long
# enough to read (and, in the headless run, to screenshot). The fake cloud transcribes nothing, so no
# "You said" line appears; its replies say they are the fake cloud's ("Answered by the fixed replies").

# Boot: the clock, with the alerts in force (configuration 1: vibration and speech).
expect spoke Sophi is on.
expect link online
expect screen ambient
wait 4000

# 1. Ask: Listening while Talk is held, One moment while the turn is with the (fake) cloud, then the reply
# as captions, then back to the clock.
key t
expect screen listening
wait 1500
key t
expect screen thinking
expect screen answering
expect 30000 screen ambient
wait 1500

# 2. Change a setting: the fake cloud offers short sounds; the captions give way to Sophi's offer
# (Confirm lit); Confirm shows Done with the new alerts, then the clock.
key t
expect screen listening
wait 1500
key t
expect screen thinking
expect screen answering
expect 40000 screen model_offer
wait 2000
key c
expect screen done
expect config 2
expect 10000 screen ambient
wait 1500

# 3. Obstacle: a hand in front of the simulated ToF. "Something close", Front left, 30 cm, Simulated.
key n
expect screen obstacle
wait 2000
key f
expect 5000 screen ambient
wait 1500

# 4. Offline: "No internet"; a Talk press there gets the walker's own line as captions; then back online.
key o
expect link offline
expect 30000 screen offline
wait 2000
key t
expect screen answering
expect 40000 screen offline
wait 1500
key o
expect link online
expect 30000 screen ambient
wait 2000
key q
